# The SDD workspace is scratch by default: review packages and generated diffs are
# regenerable from git and stay out of the repository.
*
!*/
!.gitignore

# The prose is not scratch, and treating it as such was a mistake this session had to
# discover twice. Every dispatch is cited as binding by the lane executing it; every
# report is what the next task is explicitly told to read first; every review is what a
# fix round is written against; the ledger is the recovery map after a context loss.
# An untracked file has no index, no diff, no history and no protection against a
# concurrent overwrite -- so none of the shared-file rules these documents themselves
# state can apply to them, and a paragraph one lane overwrites is gone with nothing to
# report it. Past loss here is permanently unverifiable, which is the argument for
# closing it rather than evidence that it bit us.
#
# `review-*.diff` stays ignored deliberately: it is the larger half of this directory
# by bytes and the only regenerable one (`git diff A..B`).
# By KIND, not by naming convention: `!task-*.md` was itself an enumeration -- of the
# one convention that existed the day it was written -- and it left three files behind,
# including the generator that makes the tracked briefs auditable at all.
!*.md
!*.sh
